MASTER PROJECT SPECIFICATION

WhatsApp Multi-Session Management System Controlled Through Telegram

Act as a senior software architect, expert TypeScript/Node.js engineer, Telegram Bot API developer, and WhatsApp Web integration specialist.

Your task is to DESIGN, IMPLEMENT, TEST, and DOCUMENT a complete, functional, production-oriented application that allows an authorized administrator to manage multiple WhatsApp account sessions through an interactive Telegram bot.

Do not build only a visual mockup. Implement the actual backend, Telegram interactions, session management, persistence, task execution, error handling, and deployment configuration.

Do not claim that a feature works unless it has been implemented and its behavior can be verified.

The application must be modular, maintainable, secure, and extensible.

---

1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Build a Telegram bot that serves as a centralized control panel for multiple WhatsApp accounts linked through the Baileys library.

The administrator interacts with Telegram buttons and guided workflows. The backend manages the linked WhatsApp sessions and executes supported operations through the selected sessions.

The application must support:

- Linking multiple WhatsApp accounts.
- Generating pairing codes when supported.
- Persisting and restoring authenticated sessions.
- Monitoring connection status.
- Selecting one or multiple sessions for an operation.
- Executing independent tasks concurrently.
- Sending text messages and supported media or files.
- Managing groups where the connected account has the necessary permissions.
- Joining groups when the operation is supported and authorized.
- Tracking task progress and returning results.
- Adding future operations without redesigning the entire application.

The bot must NOT use an AI model at runtime. All operations must be handled by explicit application logic, configured commands, and supported APIs.

Google AI Studio is a development tool only, not a runtime dependency.

